    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="1115" n="1109" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1109"/>

                <head>No. 30.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. J. A. King to Mr. Blount.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of the Interior</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your note of to-day’s date asking what number of citizens were naturalized in
                    these islands between 1860 and 1878, and to say in reply that the records of
                    this department show the total number of foreigners naturalized between January
                    1, 1860, and December 31, 1878, to be 750.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A. King</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister of the Interior.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">James H. Blount</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United Mates Envoy Extraordinary and Minister
                            Plenipotentiary, Honolulu.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
